+#### Constant definitions and substitutes
+
+A constant definition TLC fails to compute as it starts, it keeps as written and evaluates where
+it is used (`SpecProcessor.processConstantDefns` swallows the failure), so it applies a function
+the definition constructs lazily, where the engine builds it. Where the engine's search then
+fails, the binary declines (`the body of a function TLC keeps lazy`), as in
+`prove-it-cli/tests/startup-failures`. A definition TLC does compute is applied as the
+`FcnRcdValue` it built.
+
+A definition the configuration substitutes for a constant or a definition (`C <- f`,
+`f <- f2`) TLC evaluates as written each time it reads the name, not as the value it computed as
+it started (`Spec.lookup` gives the substitute's `OpDefNode`), and its replay's `CallStackTool`
+gives what it builds a source. The binary does the same. A function so applied outside its
+domain declines (`applied a function outside its domain`), as in
+`prove-it-cli/tests/constant-substitutes`.
+
+A failure in the body of a definition that an INSTANCE with substitutions copies, read by the
+instance's name, declines where TLC prints its call stack (`a call stack through an INSTANCE's
+substitutions`). That stack holds the `SubstInNode` SANY wraps the body in, at the INSTANCE, which
+the IR doesn't keep; the binary printed it without that frame before. The same definition read by
+its own name, as a root module that extends the module it instantiates reads it (MCetcdraft),
+has no such frame and prints as TLC does (`prove-it-cli/tests/instance-substitutions`).
+
+TLC computes no definition of a module an INSTANCE gives parameters to as it starts
+(`ModuleNode.processConstantDefns`), so a function such a definition constructs, read inside the
+module, TLC applies lazily; the one the root module names by the instance's name it computes as
+the root's. The binary reads it as TLC does, and a function so applied outside its domain declines,
+as in `prove-it-cli/tests/unprocessed-instances`.
+
+TLC computes no definition as it starts whose level it bounds above constant, which it does for
+an application of any name a state variable has, a parameter's or a bound name's too
